      "evidenceClass": "official source capability",
      "finding": "Offline FFT/iSTFT normalizes overlap-add by the summed squared window and removes centered padding; online uses direct DFT and its own overlap-add. These implementation differences prevent asserting bit identity from the shared checkpoint alone."
