  "interpretation": {
    "vad": "Observed packetization-dependent segments are supported by call-level native wrapper aggregation. A deterministic host adapter feeding at mostone512-sample-shift frame per invocation can decouple native segmentation from arbitrary capture callbacks; production integration and end-to-end timing remain unqualified.",
    "dpdf": "Offline reflected startup versus online zero startup is a verified source/artifact configuration difference. It is a plausible explanation for greater divergence on energetic hard starts, not a causally isolated explanation of the measured numerical differences.",
    "scope": "Source/artifact inspection only in this evidence record. No new model runs. No paper speedup or quality claim.",
    "timestamps": "VAD SpeechSegment.start is an absolute sample offset in accepted native input. Benchmark intersects native intervals with real input range and subtracts explicit64-sample initial context. Detected callback count is not speech duration."
  }
